# Service scheduler request collection (the frontend stub, Section 7).
#
# Written for the VS Code REST Client extension (named requests feed the
# appointment id into the get and cancel calls). Run against a seeded stack:
#   make up && make migrate && make seed
# then send the requests top to bottom.
#
# Idempotency keys live for 24 hours. To run the whole story again within a
# day, change @date to another future weekday and @run to any new value.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@apiKey = dev-api-key
@run = 1
@date = 2027-03-02

# Seed data (internal/seed): Islington Service Centre, Europe/London,
# open Monday to Friday 08:00-18:00 and Saturday 09:00-13:00, three bays.
@dealership = 01990000-0000-7000-8000-000000000102
@oilChange = 01990000-0000-7000-8000-000000000401
@olivia = 01990000-0000-7000-8000-000000000503
@oliviasFord = 01990000-0000-7000-8000-000000000604
@samuel = 01990000-0000-7000-8000-000000000504
@samuelsGolf = 01990000-0000-7000-8000-000000000605

### Liveness: no API key needed
GET {{baseUrl}}/healthz

### Readiness: database reachable and migrations applied
GET {{baseUrl}}/readyz

### Availability: free oil-change starts on @date, in UTC
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/dealerships/{{dealership}}/availability?serviceTypeId={{oilChange}}&date={{date}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Booking: 201 with the assigned bay and technician
# @name book
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/appointments
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Idempotency-Key: run-{{run}}-first
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dealershipId": "{{dealership}}",
  "customerId": "{{olivia}}",
  "vehicleId": "{{oliviasFord}}",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{oilChange}}",
  "startsAt": "{{date}}T10:00:00Z"
}

### Idempotent replay: same key and body, 200 with the same appointment
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/appointments
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Idempotency-Key: run-{{run}}-first
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dealershipId": "{{dealership}}",
  "customerId": "{{olivia}}",
  "vehicleId": "{{oliviasFord}}",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{oilChange}}",
  "startsAt": "{{date}}T10:00:00Z"
}

### Same key, different body: 422 (Idempotency-Key reused)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/appointments
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Idempotency-Key: run-{{run}}-first
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dealershipId": "{{dealership}}",
  "customerId": "{{olivia}}",
  "vehicleId": "{{oliviasFord}}",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{oilChange}}",
  "startsAt": "{{date}}T11:00:00Z"
}

### Second booking for the same time: 201 in another bay
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/appointments
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Idempotency-Key: run-{{run}}-second
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dealershipId": "{{dealership}}",
  "customerId": "{{samuel}}",
  "vehicleId": "{{samuelsGolf}}",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{oilChange}}",
  "startsAt": "{{date}}T10:00:00Z"
}

### Third booking for the same time: 201 in the last bay
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/appointments
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Idempotency-Key: run-{{run}}-third
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dealershipId": "{{dealership}}",
  "customerId": "{{samuel}}",
  "vehicleId": "{{samuelsGolf}}",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{oilChange}}",
  "startsAt": "{{date}}T10:00:00Z"
}

### Conflict: all three bays are taken, 409 with reason and suggestedStarts
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/appointments
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Idempotency-Key: run-{{run}}-fourth
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dealershipId": "{{dealership}}",
  "customerId": "{{olivia}}",
  "vehicleId": "{{oliviasFord}}",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{oilChange}}",
  "startsAt": "{{date}}T10:00:00Z"
}

### Fetch the first booking
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/appointments/{{book.response.body.$.id}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Cancel it: 200, status cancelled, its bay is free again
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/appointments/{{book.response.body.$.id}}/cancel
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Cancel again: 200 with the same state (idempotent)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/appointments/{{book.response.body.$.id}}/cancel
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### The freed bay takes a new booking for the same time: 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/appointments
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Idempotency-Key: run-{{run}}-after-cancel
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dealershipId": "{{dealership}}",
  "customerId": "{{olivia}}",
  "vehicleId": "{{oliviasFord}}",
  "serviceTypeId": "{{oilChange}}",
  "startsAt": "{{date}}T10:00:00Z"
}

### Missing API key: 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/dealerships/{{dealership}}/availability?serviceTypeId={{oilChange}}&date={{date}}

### Prometheus metrics: no API key needed
GET {{baseUrl}}/metrics
